## Who this is for

Head office is for people who run a *group* of institutes rather than one of them. There are two
such roles:

- **Organisation admin** — runs one customer's school group.
- **Super admin** — internal platform staff.

Both read the same group reports. The difference is reach: how many branches the account resolves
to. A super admin additionally gets the **Platform** screens described below.

{% callout type="note" %}
A head-office account is confined to this section. If you sign in expecting a normal staff
dashboard and land in **Group Overview** instead, nothing has gone wrong — that account is
head-office, and the ordinary per-branch screens are deliberately out of reach for it. Day-to-day
work in a single branch needs a staff account for that branch.
{% /callout %}

## Group Overview and the reports beneath it

**Group Overview** is the landing page. Beneath it sit the group-wide views, each the same question
a single branch would ask, but answered across every branch you can see:

- **Branches** — the institutes in your group.
- **Teachers**, **Accounting**, **Analytics**, **Collections**, **Operations**, **Exams**,
  **Admissions** and **Demographics** — group-level reporting for each of those areas.

These are read-across-the-group reports. Changing something for one branch still happens inside
that branch, by someone with access to it.

## Configuration

Two group-level settings live apart from the reports:

- **Discounts** — discount configuration applied across the group.
- **Term Dates** — the group's term calendar.

## Platform screens (super admin only)

**Organisations** and **Provision Branch** are internal platform work — creating a new customer
organisation, and standing up a new branch inside one. An organisation admin doesn't see these
even though they see everything above, and the restriction is enforced on the server as well as
hidden in the interface, so it isn't something that can be worked around by going to the address
directly.

